  ("Fig. 2. Set-to-set alignment (literally: (a) ‘device of writing’, (b, c) ‘is worth a cap to him’)." 0.1023 0.8981 0.2490 0.2614 0.2613 0.0125 0.0073 0.2925 0.0346)
  ("The dotted lines mark single hyperarcs." 0.1023 0.4324 0.2646 0.2771 0.2771 0.0125 0.0052 0.2833 0.0325)
  ("However, in more complex cases a whole set of text elements are translated by an-" 0.1246 0.9026 0.3108 0.3247 0.3247 0.0138 0.0065 0.3099 0.0909)
  ("other set of elements, while this correspondence cannot be broken down into pair-" 0.0981 0.9026 0.3283 0.3421 0.3421 0.0138 0.0093 0.2325 0.0476)
  ("wise correspondences of individual elements, as shown in Fig. 2. In Fig. 2 (a), one" 0.0981 0.9026 0.3458 0.3596 0.3596 0.0138 0.0090 0.2583 0.0424)
  ("word is translated by a whole run of words. In Fig. 2 (b), a whole run is translated by" 0.0981 0.9027 0.3632 0.3770 0.3770 0.0138 0.0068 0.2934 0.0475)
  ("another run, while there is no pair-wise translation correspondences between the indi-" 0.0981 0.9020 0.3807 0.3945 0.3945 0.0138 0.0065 0.2631 0.0694)
  ("vidual words in these two runs. Finally, Fig. 2 (c) shows the most general case: the" 0.0981 0.9023 0.3981 0.4119 0.4119 0.0138 0.0084 0.2673 0.0578)
  ("correspondence holds between (non-contiguous) sets of elements." 0.0981 0.7094 0.4154 0.4292 0.4292 0.0138 0.0059 0.2552 0.1459)
  ("While the structure shown in Fig. 1 can be formalized by a graph, the structure" 0.1246 0.9023 0.4328 0.4467 0.4467 0.0138 0.0093 0.2698 0.0568)
  ("shown in Fig. 2 (c) is formalized by a generalization of the notion of a graph called" 0.0981 0.9024 0.4503 0.4641 0.4641 0.0138 0.0079 0.2465 0.0604)
  ("hypergraph. Given a set of vertices V, a hypergraph G on V is defined as a graph" 0.0981 0.9030 0.4678 0.4816 0.4814 0.0138 0.0090 0.2321 0.1146)
  ("whose vertices are non-empty subsets of V, a hyperarc a being a pair of subsets of V:" 0.0981 0.9024 0.4852 0.4990 0.4988 0.0138 0.0065 0.2801 0.0590)
  ("a = {X, Y}, X, Y ⊆ V, X, Y ≠ ∅. A hyperarc can be graphically represented by a link" 0.0981 0.9025 0.4992 0.5189 0.5176 0.0138 0.0062 0.3701 0.0116)
  ("with several “ends”, as in Fig. 2 (c), or in a simplified form as a connection between" 0.0981 0.9025 0.5212 0.5350 0.5350 0.0138 0.0072 0.2857 0.0412)
  ("grouped vertices, as in Fig. 2 (a, b). The bilingual text alignment task deals with bi-" 0.0981 0.9025 0.5385 0.5523 0.5521 0.0138 0.0078 0.2714 0.0760)
  ("partite hypergraphs. A (hyper)graph is called bipartite if its vertices are of two kinds:" 0.0981 0.9024 0.5559 0.5698 0.5696 0.0138 0.0067 0.2601 0.0619)
  ("V = A ∪ B, A ∩ B = ∅, and arcs connect elements of different kinds: X ⊆ A, Y ⊆ B." 0.0981 0.8934 0.5700 0.5896 0.5883 0.0138 0.0059 0.4107 0.0167)
  ("The peculiarities of the task depend on the text units considered: words (as in our" 0.1246 0.9025 0.5919 0.6058 0.6058 0.0138 0.0075 0.2356 0.0362)
  ("examples) 12, clauses 10, sentences 146, paragraphs, sections, etc.; see Fig. 3." 0.0981 0.8242 0.6094 0.6232 0.6232 0.0138 0.0059 0.2734 0.0953)
  ("If the units are too large, such as whole sections, the task is usually trivial: the text" 0.1246 0.9024 0.6268 0.6407 0.6407 0.0138 0.0067 0.2563 0.0155)
  ("and its translation consist of the same number of sections, which correspond to each" 0.0981 0.9025 0.6443 0.6581 0.6581 0.0138 0.0076 0.2564 0.0334)
  ("other in the natural order. On the other hand, if the text units are too small—such as" 0.0981 0.9025 0.6617 0.6756 0.6756 0.0138 0.0075 0.2994 0.0476)
  ("morphemes or words—the very definition of the task becomes complicated, as Fig. 2" 0.0981 0.9026 0.6790 0.6928 0.6928 0.0138 0.0070 0.3270 0.1084)
  ("shows. In particular, in this case there are elements without translations, as in" 0.0981 0.9024 0.6965 0.7103 0.7103 0.0138 0.0129 0.2718 0.0636)
  ("Fig. 1 (a), the order of the elements is not preserved, as in Fig. 1 (b), or even the indi-" 0.0981 0.9022 0.7139 0.7278 0.7278 0.0138 0.0063 0.2842 0.0367)
  ("visible groups of elements may be not contiguous, as in Fig. 2 (c)." 0.0981 0.7128 0.7314 0.7452 0.7452 0.0138 0.0059 0.3077 0.0616)
  ("The medium-size units such as sentences and paragraphs are an intermediate" 0.1246 0.9027 0.7488 0.7627 0.7627 0.0138 0.0123 0.2290 0.0362)
  ("case: while the alignment task is not trivial, it does not usually present most of the" 0.0981 0.9022 0.7661 0.7799 0.7799 0.0138 0.0086 0.2658 0.0462)
