  ("graphs being aligned with one paragraph. Note that at least one of the two T_{X} [a .. b]" 0.0981 0.9028 0.1741 0.1890 0.1878 0.0138 0.0076 0.2717 0.0617)
  ("consists of only one paragraph, according to the conditions from Section 0. In Fig. 6," 0.0981 0.9027 0.1916 0.2054 0.2054 0.0138 0.0070 0.2589 0.0735)
  ("arbitrary values such as 0.3 are shown only to indicate that the corresponding cells" 0.0981 0.9028 0.2090 0.2228 0.2228 0.0138 0.0086 0.2103 0.0803)
  ("have been already filled by the step of calculating a_{ij}." 0.0981 0.5920 0.2265 0.2414 0.2401 0.0138 0.0057 0.2805 0.0435)
  ("As in any dynamic programming algorithm, the value a_{ij} is the total weight of the" 0.1246 0.9026 0.2439 0.2589 0.2576 0.0138 0.0073 0.3274 0.0258)
  ("optimal alignment of the initial i paragraphs of the text in the language A with the" 0.0981 0.9023 0.2614 0.2752 0.2750 0.0138 0.0089 0.2658 0.0709)
  ("initial j paragraphs of the text in the language B. Specifically, upon termination of the" 0.0981 0.9025 0.2787 0.2925 0.2923 0.0138 0.0065 0.2799 0.0539)
  ("algorithm, the bottom-right cell (marked by “?” in Fig. 6) contains the total weight of" 0.0981 0.9026 0.2961 0.3099 0.3099 0.0138 0.0067 0.3117 0.0960)
  ("the optimal alignment of the whole texts. The alignment itself is printed out by restor-" 0.0981 0.9025 0.3136 0.3274 0.3274 0.0138 0.0062 0.3242 0.0281)
  ("ing the sequence of the assignments that led to this cell:" 0.0981 0.6159 0.3310 0.3448 0.3448 0.0138 0.0059 0.2881 0.0295)
  ("5. (i,j) := (N_{A}, N_{B})." 0.2228 0.4120 0.3667 0.3816 0.3803 0.0138 0.0060 0.4924 0.0175)
