  ("(i,j) := (x,y)" 0.2959 0.4036 0.4548 0.4687 0.4687 0.0138 0.0060 0.2808 0.0342)
  ("Here, again, the minimum is sought over the same ┘-shaped area to the left and" 0.1246 0.9021 0.4876 0.5043 0.5043 0.0138 0.0084 0.2822 0.0510)
  ("above the current cell (i,j). Upon termination, this algorithm will print (in the reverse" 0.0981 0.9024 0.5079 0.5218 0.5218 0.0138 0.0070 0.3053 0.0553)
  ("order) all pairs of the sets of paragraphs in the optimal alignment. Note again that in" 0.0981 0.9025 0.5254 0.5392 0.5392 0.0138 0.0072 0.2762 0.0570)
  ("each pair at least one of the two sets consists of only one paragraph. We omit here the" 0.0981 0.9023 0.5427 0.5565 0.5565 0.0138 0.0062 0.3127 0.0426)
  ("proof of optimality, which is quite standard for dynamic programming algorithms." 0.0981 0.8635 0.5601 0.5739 0.5739 0.0138 0.0059 0.3365 0.0506)
  ("5 Complexity Analysis" 0.0981 0.3788 0.6058 0.6222 0.6222 0.0164 0.0209 0.3486 0.0140)
  ("In this paper our goal was to prove that the task of finding the exact optimal align-" 0.0981 0.9026 0.6439 0.6578 0.6578 0.0138 0.0083 0.2382 0.0194)
  ("ment is tractable, and present the general idea of the algorithm. We did not have the" 0.0981 0.9024 0.6614 0.6752 0.6752 0.0138 0.0075 0.2938 0.0463)
  ("goal of discussing its fast implementation." 0.0981 0.4903 0.6788 0.6927 0.6927 0.0138 0.0058 0.3179 0.0400)
  ("The algorithm as presented here has the complexity O(N ^{4}), where N = N_{A} ≈ N_{B} is" 0.1246 0.9027 0.6929 0.7125 0.7112 0.0138 0.0075 0.3130 0.0362)
  ("the size of the text to be aligned. Indeed, the chart contains O(N ^{2}) cells, calculating of" 0.0981 0.9028 0.7116 0.7287 0.7285 0.0138 0.0062 0.2859 0.0282)
  ("each cell requires O(N ) calculations of similarity between one paragraph and a set of" 0.0981 0.9030 0.7321 0.7459 0.7458 0.0138 0.0069 0.2761 0.0426)
  ("paragraphs, which in turn can require O(N ) comparisons of individual words. We" 0.0981 0.9023 0.7496 0.7634 0.7632 0.0138 0.0098 0.2847 0.1076)
  ("assume that the size of a paragraph and the number of translations for a word in the" 0.0981 0.9022 0.7670 0.7808 0.7808 0.0138 0.0076 0.2502 0.0680)
  ("dictionary are O(1)." 0.0981 0.2822 0.7845 0.7983 0.7981 0.0138 0.0059 0.2936 0.0945)
  ("The algorithm can be trivially modified to have the complexity O(N ^{3.5}). Indeed, the" 0.1246 0.9028 0.7987 0.8158 0.8156 0.0138 0.0059 0.3432 0.0362)
  ("Heaps law 2 states that the number of different word types in a text of length N is" 0.0981 0.9025 0.8194 0.8332 0.8330 0.0138 0.0087 0.2592 0.0581)
  ("O(N^{0.5}). Assuming a faster implementation of the algorithm from Section 0 dealing" 0.0981 0.9028 0.8334 0.8505 0.8503 0.0138 0.0084 0.3283 0.0400)
  ("with word vectors and not with individual tokens, we get the complexity of the" 0.0981 0.9023 0.8541 0.8679 0.8679 0.0138 0.0114 0.2595 0.0412)
  ("function Similarity (T_{A}, T_{B}) to be O(N^{0.5}) instead of O(N). In case of our suggested" 0.0981 0.9025 0.8683 0.8865 0.8852 0.0138 0.0082 0.2957 0.0774))
  (8
  ("Alignment of Paragraphs in Bilingual Texts" 0.4564 0.8233 0.0439 0.0564 0.0564 0.0125 0.0053 0.3204 0.0894)
  ("831" 0.8706 0.9022 0.0439 0.0564 0.0564 0.0125 nil 0.0000 0.0316)
  ("distance measure, the complexity can be even lowered to O(N ^{3}) by incremental calcula-" 0.0981 0.9026 0.0838 0.1008 0.1007 0.0138 0.0059 0.3239 0.0742)
  ("tion of the distance in the inner loop of the algorithm, due to linearity of our measure." 0.0981 0.8730 0.1045 0.1183 0.1183 0.0138 0.0054 0.3197 0.0353)
  ("In practice, the complexity can be lowered to O(N^{2}) by limiting the size of the" 0.1246 0.9026 0.1187 0.1358 0.1356 0.0138 0.0093 0.2768 0.0193)
  ("┘-shaped area in the chart calculation (which will also reduce to O(1) the calculation" 0.0981 0.9027 0.1365 0.1532 0.1530 0.0138 0.0070 0.2745 0.0886)
  ("of the similarity function). Indeed, as reported in 8, the correspondences longer that 1" 0.0981 0.9026 0.1568 0.1707 0.1707 0.0138 0.0068 0.2577 0.0194)
  ("to 3 paragraphs are low-probable." 0.0981 0.4114 0.1741 0.1879 0.1879 0.0138 0.0060 0.2589 0.0180)
  ("We even believe that a linear on average (though not in the worst case) algorithm" 0.1246 0.9026 0.1916 0.2054 0.2054 0.0138 0.0073 0.2672 0.0323)
  ("can be constructed, but this should be a topic of a future research." 0.0981 0.7074 0.2090 0.2228 0.2228 0.0138 0.0059 0.2549 0.0323)
